  "changes": [
    [
      "Opaque pearl ribbons over a glowing mosaic core instead of the sketch's clear glass",
      "R337 (Ryan, Nov 19): the Glasswright finish is opaque reflective pearl with glowing stained-glass panels; nothing see-through."
    ],
    [
      "The cleft is a short deep groove over a core of seafoam stored light, not an opening through the ship",
      "Nothing see-through; the pick asks for a short glowing cleft with the ribbons pressed together elsewhere."
    ],
    [
      "The lobes stay level amidships and turn about 77 degrees each way toward bow and stern",
      "Keeps one clear long axis and a leaf outline from above at the battle camera (the small-hull habit, frigate.md)."
    ],
    [
      "Shard F is three short drawn needles grown from the bow on the centreline",
      "The sketch's bow spikes; data.js shard fires three shots, one per needle; grown, never a tube or a crystal."
    ],
    [
      "One stern drive optic with a white bloom and a rose-cut face",
      "Family language (CD5); no flame."
    ]
